d with therapeutic success and adverse events, and to evaluate potential microbiome-based interventions to improve clinical outcomes.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a84c70da599a192104b09297\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome and the host immune system, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (ICIs). It covers preclinical mechanisms and clinical observations across various solid tumors, primarily melanoma and non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC), while also addressing methodological challenges and future interventional strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::671f0dd98d7293b1c5de958f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This article is a comprehensive review that synthesizes current knowledge on how the gut microbiota influences the efficacy and toxicity of cancer immunotherapy. It begins by outlining the biological basis of anti-tumor immunity and ICI resistance, then details the crosstalk between gut microbes and the immune system through metabolites and surface molecules. The core of the paper summarizes clinical evidence linking specific microbial signatures to ICI response in melanoma and lung cancer, highlighting both consistent trends and conflicting data. Finally, it discusses strategies for manipulating the microbiome (diet, probiotics, FMT) and identifies critical pitfalls in current research, such as heterogeneity, sampling issues, and lack of standardized protocols, proposing multi-omic approaches and rigorous trial designs for future studies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ff636bb09c91900788dba364\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"The associations are largely correlative and vary by cancer type and ICI class. The review explicitly notes conflicts in the literature regarding specific taxa (e.g., *Bacteroides*), so these should not be taken as universal rules without considering study-specific contexts.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Summarizes clinical evidence linking specific microbial signatures to ICI response in solid tumors. It lists taxa associated with improved outcomes (e.g., *Bifidobacterium*, *Faecalibacterium*, *Akkermansia*) and those linked to resistance or conflicting results (e.g., certain *Bacteroides* species). It also notes the general association between higher alpha-diversity and better response.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6362a792e1c5e373bfb230dc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical mouse models (e.g., germ-free mice, syngeneic tumor models). While plausible, direct translation to human physiology requires caution. The review distinguishes between preclinical evidence and clinical observations.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the biological mechanisms by which gut microbiota influence anti-tumor immunity. Key mechanisms include: (1) Metabolite production (e.g., inosine from *B. pseudolongum* activating A2AR signaling to enhance T-cell function; SCFAs influencing DC maturation and Treg polarization); (2) Surface molecule interactions (e.g., LPS triggering TLRs; PSA modulating Tregs); (3) Modulation of the tumor microenvironment (TME) via induction of pro-inflammatory cytokines (IFN-gamma, IL-12) and suppression of immunosuppressive cells (Tregs, MDSCs).\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::32e62e3e492f85b841f96004\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Most interventional data are from small-scale studies or ongoing trials. Long-term safety and efficacy of FMT and probiotics in cancer patients are not yet fully established. The review emphasizes the need for larger, randomized controlled trials.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Evaluates the potential of microbiome manipulation strategies (diet, probiotics, FMT, BCT) to enhance ICI efficacy. It reviews ongoing clinical trials and preliminary results, such as FMT from responders improving outcomes in melanoma patients.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de2428812c6d732ea74cd0c2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of methodological pitfalls including sample handling, lack of standardization, confounding factors (diet, antibiotics, demographics), and the difference between stool and tissue microbiota.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9c07444f0c3ecf2b3eea4f55\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Overview of the cancer immunity cycle and ICI resistance mechanisms (host-related, tumor-intrinsic, environmental).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::70f572b3471b6818dfa56246\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review covers multiple solid tumor types, but most detailed clinical data are for melanoma and NSCLC. Findings may not generalize to all solid tumors.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6987372e152f4c3d942f37c6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Conflicting results for certain bacterial genera (e.g., *Bacteroides*) are highlighted; do not assume a single direction of effect without specifying the context (species, ICI type, patient cohort).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a68b80285f0c187259d974ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Mechanistic insights are often based on preclinical models; distinguish between proven human mechanisms and hypothesized pathways supported by animal data.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a9a907e359900629c7dc170\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Interventional strategies (FMT, probiotics) are largely investigational; avoid presenting them as standard of care.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::83a8637ae312a5f8bb50d396\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e8145e70a7d1810760361df\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::98e4d7145d8aa32053893296\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::46d68237e826a20ae646f40e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用系统综述方法。1. 检索策略：基于PRISMA指南，在PubMed、WoS、Scopus进行文献检索，不限语言，截止日期为2025年1月。2. 纳入标准：成人mRCC患者，接受微生物组干预（抗生素、益生菌、前体、饮食、FMT）并与标准护理对比，报告ORR、PFS、OS或irAEs等临床终点。排除非比较研究、混合肿瘤类型未分层、儿科、临床前及非原创出版物。3. 质量评估：观察性研究使用纽卡斯尔-渥太华量表（NOS），RCT使用Cochrane RoB 2工具。4. 数据综合：定性综合各研究的干预措施、微生物组变化及临床结果，按干预类型（抗生素负面影响、益生菌/FMT潜在正面影响）分类叙述。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bb6258bf28f71234e7b1005d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"首次系统汇总mRCC领域关于微生物组干预的临床证据，明确了抗生素对ICI疗效的负面关联，以及益生菌/FMT在靶向治疗和免疫治疗中的潜在增效作用。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给材料未交代具体的荟萃分析统计结果（如合并效应量），主要依赖定性综合。证据基础薄弱：包含3项回顾性研究（存在混杂偏倚风险）和3项小样本RCT/摘要（统计效能不足，其中一项仅为会议摘要）。微生物组检测方法异质性高，缺乏标准化。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6a3d928b5a7bb7e7256aa430\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"mRCC患者接受ICI治疗，围治疗期（ICI开始前8周至开始后4周或30天内）使用广谱抗生素\",\n          \"finding\": \"抗生素暴露导致肠道菌群失调，显著降低ORR（12.9%-34.8% vs 更高比例），缩短PFS（HR 1.96-3.10）和OS（HR 3.5），增加疾病进展风险。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9dd8c9da2bda33ccfed831a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"mRCC患者接受VEGF-TKI治疗期间补充含动物双歧杆菌的酸奶\",\n          \"finding\": \"益生菌实现100%定植，富集Akkermansia muciniphila和Barnesiella intestinihominis等有益菌属，观察到PFS延长的趋势，但未达到统计学显著差异（小样本n=20）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f13d094ffea1dd368bb1748\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"mRCC患者接受pembrolizumab + axitinib治疗，接受来自长期ICI反应者的FMT\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT组1年PFS显著高于对照组（66.7% vs 35.0%, p=0.036），ORR提高（54% vs 28%），且未增加≥3级不良事件（基于Phase II RCT摘要，n=50）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a6c7883bc90d2043e3b56081\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"mRCC患者接受cabozantinib + nivolumab治疗，补充CBM588益生菌\",\n          \"finding\": \"益生菌组ORR显著高于对照组（74% vs 20%），6个月PFS改善（84% vs 60%），伴随Ruminococcaceae富集和维生素K2合成通路增加，但双歧杆菌丰度本身无显著变化。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::501f38d3cca7db07bd78d991\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ced0c1c26f04b05aed3ae8ef\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管ICIs和VEGF-TKIs改变了mRCC的治疗格局，但原发性耐药仍频繁发生。肠道微生物组被认为是影响全身治疗疗效的关键决定因素，但目前缺乏针对mRCC这一特定瘤种的系统性临床证据汇总。本研究旨在回答：在mRCC患者中，通过抗生素、益生菌、饮食或FMT调节肠道微生物组，如何影响ICIs和VEGF-TKIs的临床疗效？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0e7aba6b220c2a791e43fff0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）成年患者，接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）或血管内皮生长因子-酪氨酸激酶抑制剂（VEGF-TKIs）全身治疗。重点考察抗生素暴露、益生菌补充、饮食干预及粪便微生物群移植（FMT）对肠道微生物组的调节及其与临床结局的关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::642fafab4bece23f70645f6d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一篇系统综述，旨在评估肠道微生物组调节对mRCC患者全身治疗疗效影响的临床证据。研究遵循PRISMA指南，检索了截至2025年1月的PubMed、Web of Science和Scopus数据库。共纳入6项研究（总N=4738），包括3项回顾性队列研究和3项前瞻性随机对照试验（含一项仅摘要的II期RCT）。研究发现，围ICI治疗期的抗生素使用显著降低客观缓解率（ORR）、无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）；而益生菌（如动物双歧杆菌）在VEGF-TKI治疗中可实现定植并富集有益菌属；来自ICI反应者的FMT联合pembrolizumab + axitinib显示出改善PFS和ORR的趋势。文章指出当前证据受限于回顾性设计、小样本和方法学异质性，呼吁开展标准化、生物标志物驱动的前瞻性RCT。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6865e04b586a5c3add0ebc0b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"mRCC患者基线特征、治疗背景（VEGF-TKI与ICI联用趋势）、抗生素使用的临床普遍性及其对免疫治疗的干扰。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1e9d144e90536397445ae3cb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"各类干预措施的定义、实施时机（如ICI开始前/后窗口期）、安全性数据（FMT无增加≥3级毒性）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5af0683da0e8542be49997c0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"对现有研究局限性的总结：回顾性设计、小样本、方法学异质性、未控制的混杂因素（PPI、类固醇、饮食）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ba7a468e5cc9bd8f1d98e49\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"证据主要来自mRCC，外推至其他实体瘤需谨慎；抗生素效应的证据多为回顾性，存在混杂；益生菌/FMT的证据来自小样本或摘要，尚需大规模验证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物组状态（特别是抗生素暴露导致的失调）与ICI疗效之间的强临床关联证据。具体显示围ICI期的抗生素使用显著降低ORR、PFS和OS。同时提供了FMT和益生菌在mRCC中改善PFS和ORR的初步临床试验数据。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::34eae2b42189c49679e5f36c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制部分大量引用临床前模型（小鼠FMT恢复敏感性），临床直接证据有限；不同研究中富集的菌属和通路不一致（如CBM588未改变双歧杆菌丰度但改善了疗效），提示机制复杂性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了微生物组介导ICI疗效的部分机制线索。提及共生菌（如A. muciniphila, B. fragilis）通过树突状细胞激活和CD8+ T细胞浸润增强ICI疗效；抗生素通过耗竭SCFA产生菌、促进病原生物扩张导致耐受性免疫微环境。还提到益生菌可能通过维生素K2合成通路和富集Ruminococcaceae发挥免疫调节作用。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4bcc98caeb15f7e1bb6dd797\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述聚焦于mRCC，虽然机制具有普适性潜力，但临床结果不能直接外推至所有实体瘤。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f83a4407259ef2d37b3555fb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"抗生素对ICI疗效的负面影响证据主要来自回顾性队列，可能存在未测量的混杂因素（如感染严重程度本身影响预后）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a012c725b412df699f0d322\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"益生菌和FMT的正面效果来自小样本RCT或会议摘要，统计效力不足，不能作为确证性证据，仅提示信号。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7b1d00f8fcd8ab1638f045a9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的机制（如Akkermansia的作用）多基于临床前模型或临床相关性，临床因果证据尚不充分。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9cf23d9e0fcaca0878be814b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"不同研究中使用的益生菌菌株、FMT供体筛选标准、测序分析方法差异巨大，直接比较需谨慎。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::788b9a81bbab3067c4100631\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0090\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8b10bf15f5c5bded90fc2550\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"source_identities\": {\n      \"P0583\": {\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"source_id\": \"source::P0583\",\n        \"aliases\": [],\n        \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n        \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n        \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\"\n      },\n      \"P0577\": {\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"source_id\": \"source::P0577\",\n        \"aliases\": [],\n        \"title\": \"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\n        \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\",\n        \"paper_id\": \"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\"\n      },\n      \"P0215\": {\n        \"source_ha